Human eligibility checklist: unique donor ID; clone nested within donor; isogenic lineage and sham clone; measured copy number/structural integrity and edited-region extent; allele/first-exon assay specificity; maturation stage and differentiation batch; absolute versus relative endpoint; functional axon/myelin assay; native replicate values and sample pairing. A two-dose contrast can test strict proportionality at measured endpoints but cannot alone identify a full response curve. Multiple clones/libraries are not independent donors.

Initial lead ranking before new discovery: measured isogenic copy-number correction with paired RNA/protein/function first; human endogenous promoter perturbation second (regulation, not CN slope); independent donor tissue comparisons third (generalizability but confounding); fibroblast arrays and mutant trafficking last. Within-background test will be locked after source/design audit and before numeric extraction if suitable native values exist; otherwise publish an endpoint-specific blocker rather than weaken requirements.

## Findings

### Bounded answer and changed position
Human dosage relevance is supported beyond rodent transfer, but none of the audited contexts identifies a donor-general, maturation-independent genomic-copy-number to functional-PMP22 curve. Retain a narrower positive claim: within a human CMT1A background, dosage-directed interventions can reduce total mature RNA/total protein and improve structural myelin-associated phenotypes. Do not call this proportional functional-protein delivery or identify saturation/proteostasis from an RNA/protein mismatch.

The current deliverable is outputs/r002/human-evidence-matrix.json (also TSV): nine explicitly audited contexts, with donor/clone, pedigree, CN assay, maturation, first-exon/allele, total protein, delivery/function and source-locator fields. These are agent-authored applicability judgments validated against immutable source inputs, not automated biological truth. Donor counts across rows overlap and must not be summed. Immutable input map: inputs/immutable-inputs.json.

### Native within-background verification
Source PMC10684506, native workbook 43856_2023_400_MOESM2_ESM.xlsx, SHA256 44128de8541d8c0d7e9b8bc089ead527af0fc90f3d49aac40ee2d1f509158add. Retrieved in the Europe PMC supplementary ZIP; extracted bytes verified against the archive. Donor HPS0426/CiRA00139 is one woman aged 40-49 with CMT1A. All relevant co-cultures use the same normal neuronal background. Primary contrast is AAV-gRNAedit versus AAV-gRNAcont, not disease versus an unrelated normal donor.

Saved inputs/analysis-plan.json before opening native replicate values; main-text directions were already known, so the analysis is explicitly retrospective source verification, not a new locked biological discovery. Numeric extraction reads immutable local object-store bytes, checks labels/cell types/finite values, never evaluates formulas, and preserves exact sheet/cell locators. No cross-assay pairing, donor bootstrap, p-values or new confidence intervals were invented.

Executed results in outputs/r002/within-background-summary.json and TSV:
- Figure 7d day-47 PMP22/GAPDH RNA: control mean 0.8495434; edit mean 0.47597001; edit/control 0.5602656792, a 43.9734% decrease. Three values per group, not three donors.
- Figure 7e day-47 PMP22/GAPDH western blot: control mean 1.45631226; edit mean 1.17982406; edit/control 0.8101449754, an 18.9855% decrease. Three values per group, not three donors.
- Figure 6a native overlap: control mean 11.2375%; edit mean 31.5675%; ratio 2.8091212458. Four values per group, not four donors. Preserve workbook label Area% of MBP co-localized with MAP2; paper also describes merged neurite length. This audit does not silently convert area to length or establish the precise denominator from that wording conflict.
All three prespecified directional checks pass and all six group means match the source's stored means. Twenty numeric source cells preserved in within-background-values.tsv. This is calculation on published measurements, not independent biological replication.

Why no slope: baseline WGS supports duplication, but editing is mosaic and qPCR/Southern/TIDE estimates differ. No matched endpoint-sample absolute CN is provided; a large interval with other genes is removed. RNA and protein are relative bulk signals with no cross-assay sample map or per-viable-Schwann-cell calibration. Survival, maturation, composition and co-deleted genes remain alternatives. Figure 6 explicitly reports no compact myelin through day 50; structural overlap is not conduction or useful PMP22 molecules. Source Figure 7e edited-versus-normal total protein still differs (native K20=0.0181, inherited source statistic, not recalculated); near-normal wording is not equivalence.

### Donor, lineage and assay audit
- PMC6612317: CS67iCMT-n4/CS67iCMT-n4.ISOC4 gives target-specific isogenic evidence. MLPA/Sanger verify the parental duplication and edited region, but TALEN disables one start-codon allele rather than removing the whole duplicated interval. RNA/total protein and inflammatory outputs respond; chemotaxis is not myelin delivery. The separate multi-donor work includes four donors in two parent-child pairs; downstream microarray/secretome comparisons selected samples with >=1.5-fold PMP22 upregulation. This cannot estimate how often buffering occurs. Microarray samples are heavily nested within two CMT1A donor clones.
- PMC10316758: CS67 organoid study reuses the TALEN lineage, not a new CMT1A donor. Day-25 RNA and TEM g-ratio/periodicity improve with the isogenic comparison and selected shRNA-2/drug conditions. Numbers of neurons and multiple differentiation batches are not donors. Mixed organoids change genotype in neuronal and non-Schwann lineages too. Small-axon hypermyelination and failure of shRNA-1 to restore p-Akt/Akt despite RNA reduction are retained contrary observations. The displayed p-Akt western blots must not be counted as matched PMP22-protein mass.
- PMC11370802: human SCP lipid phenotypes are useful but reuse CS67 lineage. Preserve source CS67i-CMT-n1 versus original n4; exact clone continuity is unresolved. ddPCR/AP3B1 at the corrected region reports 1.89 versus 2.98 copies in Supplementary Figure 6. A probe spanning a TALEN-disrupted site detects intact target copies, not independent proof of whole-CNV excision. Wells/vesicles/trajectories are nested units; transcriptome similarity to progenitors and day-35 immature SC state prevent a mature-myelin interpretation. Native full matrices were not present in the inspected supplementary inventory; availability statement is on request. No claim of failed author contact.
- PMC7050273: human first-exon-specific mature RNA elevation survives in patient skin (expanded Nanostring 32 CMT1A/11 controls), but not nascent P1/P2 initiation. Preserve the roughly proportional pilot RNA-seq result (~1.55-fold; 9/7 subjects), and the different ~2-fold normalized Nanostring result/greater CMT1A variability. Duplicate punches and carryovers are not new people. SC-marker normalization improves sampling consistency but is not measured composition/state adjustment. No paired quantitative protein.
- PMC2724915: immunogold in compact dermal myelin measures relevant localization in 20 CMT1A, six HNPP, seven controls. HNPP approximately half-normal and variable CMT1A including normal-range values are both retained. Source prose has an mm2 versus figure micrometre-squared discrepancy; do not silently correct it. No detected severity correlation is not equivalence. RNA came from 29 different CMT1A subjects, so no RNA/protein efficiency can be calculated. Genetic confirmation could be in a close relative, not every individual.
- GSE7423 source metadata: outputs/r002/GSE7423-donor-channel-map.tsv maps 12 arrays to seven donor labels. Only BAR (GSM178756/757) has PMP22 duplication; JIM (GSM178758/759) has Leu16Pro and is not a second dosage donor. Normal AAL/ETT/LEY; ETT appears twice. All use a mixed reference pool. BAR derives from plantar amputation rather than sural biopsy; mitogen-expanded cultures lack late myelination context. VALUE is log10 Cy3/Cy5, not counts. The downloaded quick-view contains 20 measurement rows/sample against 43931 declared rows, so it was used for metadata only, not DE or absence claims. BONb title versus replicate-a characteristic disagreement is preserved. No validated first-exon mapping or protein endpoint; no expression rerun justified.

