Inherited failures retained, not rerun: Nae1 relative-preservation failed (-0.0365, interval -0.241,+0.168; not equivalence); original antioxidant five-gene test untestable because measured Osgin1 failed floor; four-gene comparison retrospective; Ppp6r1/Gtf2f1/Hck failed locked Zeb2 transfers; Eed truncated CSV and HDAC3 failed Mpz estimates untestable; fixed P1 mixtures fail calibration and fractions/responding cells unidentified; rat repair compartment divergence is not neonatal replication; Figlia shared controls and GSE201623 unverified donor independence; opposing footprints do not establish synthesis versus decay, IRE1 biology not novel; PXD043917 identification is not LFQ and P7/P15 conflict persists. Older unsupported browser claims were retracted, not adopted.

## Open questions

The bounded investigation is complete with a useful non-identifiability result for the central slope, not a claim that suitable experiments cannot exist. Most discriminating next experiment: independent human donor backgrounds with independently edited and sham clones, exact genomic CN and structural integrity measured in the same endpoint preparations, matched lineage/maturation, absolute total and surface/myelin PMP22 plus RNA at multiple times, and neuronal function/conduction. Keep functional-allele inactivation separate from structural CN correction; do not select preparations by elevated PMP22. A precise two-dose ratio can test proportionality for those doses; multiple verified doses are needed to characterize response shape. Endogenous human first-exon nascent output and calibrated useful protein remain open.

